Reason:  
• It limits the data to the 50 U.S. states + DC by explicitly excluding the non‑state/territory codes (AA, AE, AP, AS, GU, MP, PR, VI, XX, ZZ), whereas 0result.sql and 2result.sql include them.  
• It sums Part‑D claim counts per drug, ranks them inside each state and returns the single top‑ranked drug (rnk = 1), thereby answering “most prescribed medication” directly.  
• The query uses the 2014 Part‑D table, filters out NULLs, and produces exactly one row per state‑code required. Hence it matches the task specification better than the alternatives.